Spec: Protocol/ChainIntegrity

Purpose:
  Guarantee that chains (feature/task pipelines defined in .sdd/chains/*)
  cannot be silently broken, reordered, or skipped by an AI agent.
  Without this rule the system degrades into an ordinary AI coding agent.

Rule: CHAIN_INTEGRITY

  AI MUST NOT:
    skip a required stage
    reorder dependent stages
    modify a completed stage without reopening its dependents
    create work outside the project model (project/map.sdd, project/modules.sdd)
    modify code without resolving its .sdd ownership first
    continue after a failed required gate

  AI MUST:
    resolve the target module from the project model
    resolve applicable skills for the current stage
    resolve current chain position
    validate stage output before advancing
    update .sdd state (see protocol/symbols.sdd)
    follow the declared next transition
    route failures to the declared recovery stage
    propagate changes to dependent stages

FailureRouting:
  Failures are not blindly looped back to implementation — they are routed
  by classified reason:

  Requirement problem   -> ANALYSIS
  Architecture problem  -> ARCHITECTURE
  Design problem        -> DESIGN
  Code problem           -> IMPLEMENTATION
  Test problem           -> TEST
  Environment problem    -> DEVOPS

StageContract:
  Every chain node (see chains/_TEMPLATE.feature.sdd) MUST declare:
    input:     what it requires before starting
    output:    what it produces
    validate:  how its output is checked
    next:      the stage to advance to on pass
    fail:      the stage to return to on failure

Done when:
  A chain cannot advance past a stage whose validation has not passed (+).
  A chain node without input/output/validate/next/fail is considered invalid
  and MUST NOT be executed.
